# Machine agent framework (Hermes)

The registry at `{{REPO_DIR}}/roles.config.json` is the single source of truth
for every agent profile on this machine. Each profile is installed here as an
`agent-<key>` skill — **including `planner` and `builder`**, which earlier
installs structurally could not contain because the installer iterated only the
specialists map.

{{ROSTER_SENTENCE}}

{{ROSTER_TABLE}}

## What Hermes can and cannot do with this framework

**Cannot: route a profile to its configured model.** Hermes's active model comes
from its own harness configuration; the model metadata in each profile records
routing intent only. A profile you adopt runs on the session's model. Say that
plainly if asked.

The `tools:` list in each profile is Claude Code's tool vocabulary and is not
enforced here, so a read-only profile's boundary is a discipline. Keep it anyway.

## Picking a profile

- **`runner`** is the everyday front door for routine work, maintenance, and triage.
- **`planner` → `builder`** is the development core; see `agent-pb`.
- **`code-reviewer`** runs before every PR — the Git Workflow Standard makes this
  mandatory on every harness. Never write "reviewed" into a PR body unless a
  review actually ran.
- Direct-call-only profiles ({{DIRECT_CALL_ONLY}}) run only when the user asks
  for them by name.

